# Maintainer: Jan Alexander Steffens (heftig) <heftig@archlinux.org>
# Contributor: Eric Bélanger <eric@archlinux.org>
#
# webkitgtk-6.0 -- the GTK4 / libsoup3 API build of WebKitGTK, with the ppc64le
# JavaScriptCore JIT port staged in prepare().
#
# DERIVED FROM ours/webkit2gtk-4.1, NOT from Arch's webkitgtk-6.0 recipe (whose
# stale 2.52.5 import sat at the top of this tree until it was retired), and
# that is deliberate. Both are the same upstream tarball and the same
# PORT=GTK; the only real difference is USE_GTK4 and the package names. Our 4.1
# recipe is the one that has been proven to build 2.54.1 on ppc64le, so 6.0 is
# generated from it and the two are kept textually close enough to diff.
#
# The tree's own webkitgtk-6.0 recipe is left alone. It is Arch POWER's, pinned
# at 2.52.5 and restricted to arch=(powerpc espresso), and it carries three
# downstream patches -- prefer-pthread, reduce-memory-overheads and
# documentloader-eventloop-h. None of those are here, because none is needed
# for this configuration: our 4.1 recipe carries none of them and builds 2.54.1
# with PORT=GTK clean, 926 of 926 edges. Two of the three would also need
# rebasing against 2.54.1 (prefer-pthread's context is the project version
# line; reduce-memory-overheads lost its USE_APPLE_ICU anchor and its
# USE_LD_GOLD guard now tests a variable that no longer exists anywhere in
# 2.54.1's cmake). They may still matter for the 32-bit powerpc targets that
# recipe serves; that is why it is untouched rather than replaced.
#
# WHO WANTS THIS: epiphany (GNOME Web) and yelp both link webkitgtk-6.0, not
# 4.1. Both already ship for ppc64le against base/webkitgtk-6.0 2.52.3, which
# is a CLoop build with no ppc64 JIT at all -- so this does not enable them, it
# makes them fast. That is also the reason to care about 6.0 separately from
# 4.1 at all: 4.1 serves the embedded-webview consumers (kicad, remmina, wx,
# artcraft, the Nautilus previewer), and 6.0 is where the actual browser lives.
#
# BUILT, PACKAGED AND RUN. webkitgtk-6.0 2.54.1-1 built first try, packaged,
# installed (pacman -U, 2026-10-10), and Epiphany 50.4 ran on it for ten
# minutes with the JIT live. No GTK4-side surprises appeared.
#
# What that run did find is the bug pkgrel 2 exists for, and it was JSC-side
# after all: a code object whose baseline machine code exceeds the +-32 MB a
# `b` reaches aborted in the jump-island allocator, because
# JIT::privateCompileLinkPass() links jumps while the code is still in the
# assembler buffer and an island needs the branch's final address in the
# executable pool. Measured on the crash: 5,578,642 label slots, ~38 MB of
# code, a -38.7 MB backward branch. Fixed in the shared port layer, so 4.1 gets
# it from the same tarball.

